Yes. At this point it’s almost certainly index.html, not waiting.

Your script.js is looking for this:

<button id="adminButton">Admin</button>

If your Admin button does not have id="adminButton", it will sit there like a decorative potato.

Also, script.js needs these IDs in index.html:

<div id="adminLoginModal" class="modal hidden">
  <div class="modal-card">
    <h2>Admin Login</h2>
    <p>This is a prototype login. Real admin accounts will be handled through Supabase later.</p>

    <input id="adminPassword" type="password" placeholder="Enter admin password" />

    <button id="adminLoginBtn">Enter Admin Dashboard</button>
    <button id="adminCancelBtn" type="button">Cancel</button>

    <small>Demo password: loopadmin</small>
  </div>
</div>

So next step:

Open index.html
Click edit
Find the admin button
Make sure it is exactly:
<button id="adminButton" class="admin-float-btn" type="button">Admin</button>

Then search the file for:

adminLoginModal

If it’s missing, we need to add the modal above the closing </body> tag.

So yes: update index.html next. CSS is just the outfit. The button currently has no nervous system.

